From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: give the camera rails their real
 ranges

The PM8009 rails added earlier were pinned to a single point each, with minimum
equal to maximum, using figures read from the stock sensor nodes rather than
from the regulators themselves. The vendor regulator description gives ranges:
1.100 to 1.304 V for ldo1 and 1.096 to 1.304 V for ldo4.

The three camera slots fed by these rails reset the handset the moment they are
powered, while the one slot fed by ldo2, described before this port touched
anything, powers up cleanly and reports its sensor. Asking an RPMh regulator for
a voltage its own description does not offer is wrong regardless of whether it
explains that.

ldo3 takes ldo4's range: it is the same NLDO and the vendor description does not
carry it separately.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi
@@ -401,8 +401,8 @@
 		vdd-l5-l6-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
 
 		vreg_l1f_1p1: ldo1 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1104000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1104000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
@@ -413,14 +413,14 @@
 		};
 
 		vreg_l3f_1p05: ldo3 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1056000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1056000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1096000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l4f_1p05: ldo4 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1056000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1056000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1096000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
--
